  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s8AAAABGM4m5w",
      "title": "params: expose EIP-8282 system contracts for L1 library consumers",
      "author": "joshklop",
      "number": 814,
      "body": "## Summary\n\nThe Optimism monorepo needs EIP-8282's canonical builder deposit/exit predeploys when generating L1 dev genesis allocations for an upstream geth subprocess. Its Go imports still resolve to op-geth, which exports the Prague queue definitions but not these two builder queues. This backport allows the consumer to use `params` consistently instead of embedding an allocation JSON fixture.\n\n- Export `BuilderDepositAddress`, `BuilderDepositCode`, `BuilderExitAddress`, and `BuilderExitCode`, copied verbatim from [released go-ethereum v1.17.7](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/v1.17.7/params/protocol_params.go).\n- Add canonical-address and fixed runtime-code SHA-256 regression tests.\n\n**Library-only scope:** no changes to genesis construction, state processing, fork activation, dependencies, or generated code. This does not implement Glamsterdam in the unsupported op-geth binary. Consumer: https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/23152.\n\n## Validation\n\n- All four exported definitions independently compared with released upstream source.\n- `go test ./params -count=1`\n- `make all`\n- `go run ./build/ci.go lint`\n- `go run ./build/ci.go check_generate`\n- `go run ./build/ci.go check_baddeps`\n- `go run ./build/ci.go test` (full repository suite, including execution-spec fixtures and keeper module)\n- Independent read-only Codex review: no findings in either params file. Its temporary test-submodule checkout observation was resolved by completing initialization to the unchanged pinned commits.\n- Consumer queue regression test and all four Glamsterdam scenarios pass with a temporary local-module override (not committed).\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-02T00:16:40Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-06T19:08:46Z",
      "additions": 70,
      "deletions": 0
    }
  ],
